  "description": "the control twin of every-nested-registration-budgeted: a single non-accumulating every with the same empty body over the same 12 ticks completes cleanly on the same instruction budget, so that fixture's ol-limit is caused by the accumulation and not merely by a budget too small for any program. THE TWO FIXTURES MUST MOVE TOGETHER: this one is clean and byte-identical at every budget from 18 upward, so its 26 is pinned only by its twin -- whose own recorded event stream changes at every budget step (13 events at 18, 19 at 26, 20 at 27), so the twin pins 26 UNIQUELY while this one merely has to agree. 'Tightening' this one to its own minimum of 18 would leave both fixtures passing while the pair silently stopped being a same-budget pair, which is the entire discrimination. 26 was re-derived from 14 by issue #953, which made each wait tick a charged instruction and so added the 12 of `wait 12` to both twins",
